			"Message": "style(Rest): Normalise shell redirect spacing and JS import grouping\n\nContinue the formatting consistency pass across Rest's shell scripts, JavaScript entry points, and documentation:\n\n- Shell scripts (Bench.sh, prepublishOnly.sh, run_tests.sh): Add space between redirect operators and their targets (`2> /dev/null`, `> \"$file\"`, `> bin/Rest.js`); normalise case label indentation within case/esac blocks; convert pipeline continuations to end-of-line backslash style.\n- JavaScript (index.js, postinstall.js): Remove blank-line separators between Node.js built-in imports; collapse blank lines at function body openings.\n- Markdown (README.md, DeepDive.md): Reflow paragraphs to consistent 100-char line width; normalise table column alignment formatting.\n- Binary (bin/Rest): Updated binary after rebuild.\n\nNo runtime behaviour changes — formatting and whitespace only. Follow-up to the previous style commit, applying additional patterns missed in the first pass.",
