			"Message": "style(Rest): Normalise whitespace, shell formatting, and doc comment line-wrapping\n\nApply formatting consistency fixes across shell scripts, Rust source, and JavaScript entry points:\n\n- Shell scripts (Bench.sh, prepublishOnly.sh, run_tests.sh): Remove spaces between redirect operators and file paths (`2>/dev/null`, `>\"$file\"`, `cat >bin/Rest.js`), normalise pipeline continuation style (pipe at end-of-line instead of start-of-line), dedent case pattern labels within case/esac blocks, and remove space after `<` in input redirects.\n- Rust source (Bundle/Builder.rs, Bundle/mod.rs, OXC/Compile.rs, SWC/Compile.rs, SWC/Watch/Compile.rs, Transform/mod.rs): Reflow doc comment paragraphs to respect 100-char line width consistently; collapse single-expression function `build_watch` onto one line.\n- JavaScript (index.js, postinstall.js): Add blank-line separators between import statements (grouping Node.js built-in imports) and at the start of function bodies for standard JS whitespace conventions.\n\nNo runtime behaviour changes — formatting and whitespace only.",
			"SHA": "bb943e98d0e0ef95a5fa9207b948b685d5212cc3"
		},
